    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72400" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴκτ-ιστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, irreg. 
			Sup. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκτρός,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>most pitiable, lamentable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴ . . . δειλοῖσι βροτοῖσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.76
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάνον οἰ. θανάτῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.412
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτθίσιν οἰκτίστη, σὸν φάος,
					Ἠριγόνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Aet.</u>
					1.1.4
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴ. δὴ κεῖνο ἴδον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					12.258
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴ. ἔλεγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.782
				</span></i>
			 : neut. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴκτιστα</span> as
				Adv., <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.472
			</span></i> : also in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Onos.
				42.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Anach.</u>
				11
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phalar.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					96
				</span></i>
			.</div>
